  "scope": "Fence Storyboard poster persistence and replace event URL adoption with authoritative detail refresh.",
  "upstreamExisting": [
    "Script poster generation/storage, native/configured models and durable checkpoints",
    "Organization wallet reservations, usage observations and idempotent debit",
    "Durable Object realtime/SSE/history, QueryClient detail and pending-launch registry"
  ],
  "implemented": [
    "One SQL UPDATE RETURNING checks organization, sequence, current root or explicitly trusted raw claim, and processing.",
    "Incurred usage/debit steps precede publication with unchanged names, identity, pricing and reservation fields.",
    "A refused publication emits nothing, releases only its payload hold and returns before child dispatch.",
    "Poster owner survives the optional schema, real DO SSE/history serialization and leaf parsing; ownerless legacy events remain accepted.",
    "Events request exact authoritative detail; their URL never writes cache. Old reads are cancelled, cold/no-observer detail is fetched and later signals require a trailing read.",
    "Pending launches retain their confirmation authority. Per-read non-manual query success distinguishes warm cancellation from an actual read.",
    "A synchronous detail-query lifetime makes cold clear/removal discard queued refreshes; subscriptions and ordinary errors have explicit cleanup."
  ],
